This file records third-party code linked into keeper that is not a cargo or
npm package, and so is not covered by `cargo deny` or the JS licence gate.
Vendored crates keep their own LICENSE and NOTICE files in their directories
(`tools/fluidaudio-rs/`, `tools/tao/`).

This file and the licence texts under `licenses/` travel inside the apps that
link the code they name, as NOTICE and licenses/: on a Mac in
keeper.app/Contents/Resources/ (Finder: Show Package Contents), on the iPhone at
the top of the app bundle. The bundle guard every install runs
(`scripts/lib/bundle-guard.sh`) refuses a built app without them, and
`scripts/bundle-notices.test.ts` fails if either bundle configuration stops
naming them.

